35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, the data confirms our fears. Broad mandates fail, but narrow, owned tools endure. We must fund the specific, not the general.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found the capital line is frozen, but the software allowance has room. Also, per-head licences keep climbing, while fixed-fee work stays stable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Whoa! Half the plants have no signal for whole afternoons? And six weeks just to get devices approved? That’s a huge trap!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, the data is clear. Four failed efforts lack owners, yet the tool room walkthroughs persist. We must fund specific, owned solutions, not broad mandates.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
